{"name":"Mock Orange","hex":"#ff9863","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mock orange","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any shrub of the genus Philadelphus, particularly Philadelphus coronarius (sweet mock orange).","Bursaria spinosa (Australian blackthorn), a small tree from Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mock_orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bursaria spinosa","blocks":[{"text":"Bursaria spinosa is a small tree or shrub in the family Pittosporaceae. The species occurs mainly in the eastern and southern half of Australia and not in Western Australia or the Northern Territory. Reaching 10 m (35 ft) high, it bears fragrant white flowers at any time of year but particularly in summer. A common understorey shrub of eucalyptus woodland, it colonises disturbed areas and fallow farmland. It is an important food plant for several species of butterflies and moths, particularly those of the genus Paralucia, and native bees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Bursaria_spinosa_flowers_and_fruit_P2150004.jpg/330px-Bursaria_spinosa_flowers_and_fruit_P2150004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bursaria_spinosa","wikidata":"Q2928619"},{"title":"Choisya ternata","blocks":[{"text":"Choisya ternata is a species of flowering plant in the family Rutaceae, known as Mexican orange blossom or Mexican orange."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Choisya_Inflorescence_FR_2013.jpg/330px-Choisya_Inflorescence_FR_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Choisya_ternata","wikidata":"Q2964355"},{"title":"Mock Orange (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Mock Orange is an American indie rock band from Evansville, Indiana, United States. They debuted in 1998 during a growing emo and punk musical climate."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mock_Orange_(band)","wikidata":"Q6887773"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bursaria_spinosa_foliage.jpg/500px-Bursaria_spinosa_foliage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bursaria_spinosa_foliage.jpg/1280px-Bursaria_spinosa_foliage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bursaria_spinosa_foliage.jpg/500px-Bursaria_spinosa_foliage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Foliage","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABursaria_spinosa_foliage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Bursaria_spinosa_subsp._lasiophylla.jpg/500px-Bursaria_spinosa_subsp._lasiophylla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Bursaria_spinosa_subsp._lasiophylla.jpg/500px-Bursaria_spinosa_subsp._lasiophylla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Habit, subsp. lasiophylla","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABursaria_spinosa_subsp